    "number": 241,
    "title": "feat(#123): implement persistent_read_without_ttl_extension lint",
    "body": "## Description\n\nImplements a new lint \\persistent_read_without_ttl_extension\\ that detects reads from \\env.storage().persistent()\\ in a contract function where no \\extend_ttl\\ call covers the same key on any path through that function.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nPersistent storage entries in Soroban expire. Once archived, the next access requires a restore operation costing substantially more than the read. A contract reading a persistent key on a hot path without extending TTL carries a latent cost cliff that local tests don't surface (local ledgers don't advance far enough to archive anything).\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Uses \\LateLintPass::check_fn\\ with a \\PersistentReadVisitor\\ that walks the function body collecting all persistent reads (\\get\\, \\has\\) and \\extend_ttl\\ calls.\n- Reuses \\match_soroban_def_path\\ / \\matches_any_path\\ from the existing shared utils (per \\#66).\n- Does **not** fire for \\\temporary()\\ or \\instance()\\ storage — their lifecycle differs.\n- Conservative analysis: reports if ANY persistent read exists without ANY \\extend_ttl\\ in the function.\n\n## Known false positives\n\n- \\extend_ttl\\ called in a helper or caller function outside the analyzed function body\n- \\extend_ttl\\ called on a different key than the read — the current analysis is function-scoped, not key-scoped\n- Reads guarded by \\has\\ checks that handle the archived case (documented but not exempted, since the pattern is uncommon)\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Action |\n|------|--------|\n| \\soroban_cost_lints/src/lib.rs\\ | Added lint declaration, \\PersistentReadWithoutTtlExtension\\ pass, \\LINT_METADATA\\ entry, pass registration |\n| \\soroban_cost_lints/ui/main.rs\\ | Added \\extend_ttl\\ to \\Persistent\\ stub, 6 test fixtures (2 bad, 4 good) |\n| \\docs/lints/persistent_read_without_ttl_extension.md\\ | Created per-lint documentation page |\n\nCloses #123",
